  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick cell_size in [3,5], num_sep_rows in [2,5], num_sep_cols in [2,6]
    2. Place separators at cell_size, 2*cell_size+1, ... for rows and cols
    3. Choose last_row_gap in [0, cell_size] and last_col_gap in [0, cell_size]
       to set grid dimensions; grid_h = last_sep_row + 1 + last_row_gap, similar for width
    4. Build output — fill bg, paint sep rows/cols with line_color=5, intersections with marker_color
    5. Build input from output — copy output, then add noise:
       a. Scatter marker_color pixels in 5-18% of cell-interior bg cells
       b. Replace 3-16% of line_color cells on sep rows/cols with marker_color
       c. Optionally replace some intersection cells back to line_color (solver tolerates this)
    6. Verify solver constraint — line_color must be uniquely identified as the color
       with max single-row/col count among foreground colors (noise must not exceed line pixels)
